274
00:10:14,967 --> 00:10:15,900
-Could be.

275
00:10:20,567 --> 00:10:21,367
-So?

276
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:22,867
[CHUCKLES]

277
00:10:25,867 --> 00:10:28,100
-Traveling at a moderate
15 miles per hour,

278
00:10:28,133 --> 00:10:30,167
we made our way
safely through space.

279
00:10:34,067 --> 00:10:34,733
-Oh, Z'No!

280
00:10:40,867 --> 00:10:42,267
-A place!

281
00:10:42,300 --> 00:10:45,100
-Here to sing his
Top-10 country hit.

282
00:10:48,300 --> 00:10:49,667
[DOOR CREAKING]

283
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:52,300
-Hey, it's William
Conrad's CAT scan machine.

284
00:10:52,333 --> 00:10:52,767
-Whew!

285
00:10:52,800 --> 00:10:54,600
-Yeah!

286
00:10:54,633 --> 00:10:56,700
-Formerly of Kazja Goo-goo.

287
00:10:56,733 --> 00:10:57,233
-You think.

288
00:10:59,867 --> 00:11:01,467
Well, they sent the
ship up, but they

289
00:11:01,500 --> 00:11:04,133
forgot to put in astronauts.

290
00:11:04,167 --> 00:11:05,000
-Names without Z's in 'em?

291
00:11:05,033 --> 00:11:07,333
What the hell?

292
00:11:07,367 --> 00:11:08,300
Aw!

293
00:11:08,333 --> 00:11:10,233
[SNORING]

294
00:11:10,267 --> 00:11:12,600
-The spaceship is handicap
accessible, that's nice.

295
00:11:12,633 --> 00:11:13,100
-Yeah.

296
00:11:13,133 --> 00:11:13,633
Hmm.

297
00:11:16,533 --> 00:11:17,333
-Patrick, wait!

298
00:11:17,367 --> 00:11:18,933
Come back and be in the movie!

299
00:11:18,967 --> 00:11:19,467
-Oh, now.

300
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:25,600
[WHIRRING]

301
00:11:25,633 --> 00:11:28,100
-I am a camera.

302
00:11:28,133 --> 00:11:29,000
Ah!

303
00:11:29,033 --> 00:11:30,500
There's a Z. We're
back on track, now.

304
00:11:30,533 --> 00:11:35,167
[YELLING AND WHIRRING]

305
00:11:35,200 --> 00:11:36,933
