-Lay that ham up there.

536
00:22:58,267 --> 00:22:58,933
-OK, but, uh--

537
00:22:58,967 --> 00:22:59,733
-There we go.

538
00:22:59,767 --> 00:23:00,867
-There's the new
legs, but I don't

539
00:23:00,900 --> 00:23:01,800
think they're gonna
be very functional.

540
00:23:01,833 --> 00:23:02,433
-That's OK.

541
00:23:02,467 --> 00:23:03,000
Thanks, Mike.

542
00:23:03,033 --> 00:23:04,167
Hello folks.

543
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:06,700
You may be wondering why I'm
not kickboxing right now.

544
00:23:06,733 --> 00:23:07,900
I apologize.

545
00:23:07,933 --> 00:23:10,667
You have every right to
expect constant kickboxing.

546
00:23:10,700 --> 00:23:13,300
But the truth is, until
recently, I had no legs.

547
00:23:13,333 --> 00:23:16,633
However, I've just remedied that
by actually making myself some.

548
00:23:16,667 --> 00:23:17,633
Ha, ha!

549
00:23:17,667 --> 00:23:19,867
So get ready for some
hot kickboxing action!

550
00:23:19,900 --> 00:23:21,433
The first poor schmo
who comes along

551
00:23:21,467 --> 00:23:24,200
is going to get a taste of my
Ashley Judd-like kickboxing

552
00:23:24,233 --> 00:23:25,100
wrath!

553
00:23:25,133 --> 00:23:27,967
-(SINGING) You shook
me all night long.

554
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,000
-Ah! a challenger!

555
00:23:29,033 --> 00:23:30,033
-Hi, Tom.

556
00:23:30,067 --> 00:23:31,167
-Ha!

557
00:23:31,200 --> 00:23:33,167
You dare to oppose me,
strange top-heavy purple one?

558
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:34,033
-What?

559
00:23:34,067 --> 00:23:35,800
-Prepare to be kickboxed
by my new legs.

560
00:23:35,833 --> 00:23:37,400
-I don't want to fight, Tom.

561
00:23:37,433 --> 00:23:38,333
I'd like you.

562
00:23:38,367 --> 00:23:39,933
-You will fight, coward!

563
00:23:39,967 --> 00:23:41,567
[STRAINING] Gosh dang it!

564
00:23:41,600 --> 00:23:42,267
Come on legs!

565
00:23:42,300 --> 00:23:44,267
-They're pretty, new legs, Tom.

566
00:23:44,300 --> 00:23:45,633
-Fawning flattery
will not help you!

567
00:23:45,667 --> 00:23:47,600
[STRAINING] Dumb,
stupidity, sticky legs!

568
00:23:47,633 --> 00:23:48,833
Oh, agh, whoa!

569
00:23:48,867 --> 00:23:49,500
Oh, boy!

570
00:23:49,533 --> 00:23:50,267
Oh, jeez.

571
00:23:50,300 --> 00:23:51,733
Aw, just a temporary setback.

572
00:23:51,767 --> 00:23:52,300
I'll--

573
00:23:52,333 --> 00:23:53,233
-Do you need help, Tom?

574
00:23:53,267 --> 00:23:53,733
-No!

575
00:23:53,767 --> 00:23:54,733
No, get-- aah.

576
00:23:54,767 --> 00:23:55,233
Aah!

577
00:23:55,267 --> 00:23:56,267
Whew!

578
00:23:56,300 --> 00:23:58,167
There, now stop your
pathetic delaying tactics.

579
00:23:58,200 --> 00:23:59,767
I insist you fight me, weakling!

580
00:23:59,800 --> 00:24:01,067
-Well, if you want.

581
00:24:01,100 --> 00:24:02,100
OK, Tom.

582
00:24:02,133 --> 00:24:02,600
-Huh?

583
00:24:02,633 --> 00:24:03,700
Oh-- oh, boy!

584
00:24:03,733 --> 00:24:04,200
-Hiya!

585
00:24:04,233 --> 00:24:06,833
-Look-- ow!

586
00:24:06,867 --> 00:24:07,767
-Sorry.

587
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:10,133
-I thought you didn't
have legs, either.

588
00:24:10,167 --> 00:24:11,367
-Just made it today.

589
00:24:11,400 --> 00:24:12,533
Neat, huh?

590
00:24:12,567 --> 00:24:14,233
We'll be right back.

591
00:24:14,267 --> 00:24:15,767
I should make another one.

592
00:24:27,967 --> 00:24:28,467
-Oh!

593
00:24:34,300 --> 00:24:35,533
[GASP]

594
00:24:35,567 --> 00:24:36,033
-Ha!

595
00:24:36,067 --> 00:24:36,667
Wow.

596
00:24:36,700 --> 00:24:40,500
Sister Vehicular Homicide.

597
00:24:40,533 --> 00:24:41,300
-Oh, great!

598
00:24:41,333 --> 00:24:44,000
Third time this week.

599
00:24:44,033 --> 00:24:46,200
I'll just a note on him.

600
00:24:46,233 --> 00:24:47,100
-Thank god, he's alive.

601
00:24:47,133 --> 00:24:49,033
Can somebody help me?

602
00:24:49,067 --> 00:24:51,033
Please, somebody help me!

603
00:24:54,967 --> 00:24:55,933
-Help me, Sister Roscoe.

604
00:24:55,967 --> 00:24:56,767
-Fred!

605
00:24:56,800 --> 00:24:57,633
Oh, Fred.

606
00:24:57,667 --> 00:24:59,300
-I'm all flibbertigibbet.

607
00:24:59,333 --> 00:25:01,733
-In the car-- a man.

608
00:25:01,767 --> 00:25:02,667
[PANTING]

609
00:25:02,700 --> 00:25:04,433
-Hair weave doesn't
blend in that well.

610
00:25:04,467 --> 00:25:05,767
-There's an injured man in car.

611
00:25:05,800 --> 00:25:08,267
He needs our help.

612
00:25:08,300 --> 00:25:09,800
-Hey, Oscar, we need
your help outside.

613
00:25:09,833 --> 00:25:13,200
-I'll loan him some flesh.

614
00:25:13,233 --> 00:25:13,700
-Ann?

615
00:25:13,733 --> 00:25:16,767
Long time no see.

616
00:25:16,800 --> 00:25:18,200
-She's wearing a
maternity habit.

617
00:25:22,433 --> 00:25:23,833
-You van is under
arrest for not having

618
00:25:23,867 --> 00:25:26,800
a scene painted on the side.

619
00:25:26,833 --> 00:25:28,967
-The van must be having
emissions problems.

620
00:25:29,000 --> 00:25:30,333
It's blackened the
lower atmosphere.

621
00:25:34,000 --> 00:25:36,000
-Hey, what have we got?

622
00:25:36,033 --> 00:25:38,400
-A homeless guy with
his throat ripped out.

623
00:25:38,433 --> 00:25:40,900
-By what?

624
00:25:40,933 --> 00:25:41,833
-Who cares?

625
00:25:41,867 --> 00:25:43,367
-Figure mountain lion,
grizzlies come out

626
00:25:43,400 --> 00:25:45,233
of the hills in search of food.

627
00:25:45,267 --> 00:25:47,500
Found this poor
bastard, instead.

628
00:25:47,533 --> 00:25:48,233
-Great.

629
00:25:48,267 --> 00:25:49,233
Just great.

630
00:25:49,267 --> 00:25:51,333
Has anybody called the
Humane Society, the zoo?

631
00:25:51,367 --> 00:25:53,800
-They're sending
some people out.

632
00:25:53,833 --> 00:25:56,433
-Captain, we've
got something here.

633
00:25:56,467 --> 00:25:57,333
-We found part of a burger.

634
00:25:57,367 --> 00:25:58,500
I want to know if
I could eat it?

635
00:26:02,033 --> 00:26:02,867
It's not that dirty.

636
00:26:02,900 --> 00:26:04,733
Split it with ya.

637
00:26:04,767 --> 00:26:06,933
-We found this.

638
00:26:06,967 --> 00:26:09,433
-What the hell made that?

639
00:26:09,467 --> 00:26:10,933
-That's your shadow, boss.

640
00:26:16,800 --> 00:26:19,333
-Jesus, I think I
should be wearing a tie.

641
00:26:19,367 --> 00:26:20,000
Ow!

642
00:26:20,033 --> 00:26:21,133
-Oh, my gout.

643
00:26:21,167 --> 00:26:22,033
-Ow.

644
00:26:22,067 --> 00:26:23,667
-I mean, don't give
me a hard time.

645
00:26:23,700 --> 00:26:24,467
OK?

646
00:26:24,500 --> 00:26:26,433
-Uh, I think you broke a bone.

647
00:26:26,467 --> 00:26:27,933
-I mean, what is this bull?

648
00:26:27,967 --> 00:26:28,600
-Hm?

649
00:26:28,633 --> 00:26:29,833
-I mean, no special favors.

650
00:26:29,867 --> 00:26:30,333
-OK.

651
00:26:30,367 --> 00:26:33,167
Anything you say.

652
00:26:33,200 --> 00:26:36,267
-And watch that language.

653
00:26:36,300 --> 00:26:37,467
-OK, OK.

654
00:26:37,500 --> 00:26:38,800
-OK, so now you don't like
my cooking, Sister. challenge

655
00:26:38,833 --> 00:26:39,300
[CHUCKLING]

656
00:26:39,333 --> 00:26:39,900
-Oh, I don't know.

657
00:26:39,933 --> 00:26:40,733
I'm just not hungry.

658
00:26:40,767 --> 00:26:41,700
Thanks for cooking.

659
00:26:41,733 --> 00:26:43,700
-Hey, I have some
nice, chocolate cake,

660
00:26:43,733 --> 00:26:44,933
some mocha almond ice cream.

661
00:26:44,967 --> 00:26:46,000
-Hey, I'll have some.

662
00:26:46,033 --> 00:26:46,500
-No, thanks.

663
00:26:46,533 --> 00:26:47,400
I think I'll pass.

664
00:26:47,433 --> 00:26:49,100
-It's a halfway
house for huge guys.

665
00:26:51,600 --> 00:26:52,933
-This is worse than I thought.

666
00:26:52,967 --> 00:26:54,200
-There's no butter in my coffee.

667
00:26:57,367 --> 00:26:59,733
-You're at home now, Annie.

668
00:26:59,767 --> 00:27:02,733
So what's going on?

669
00:27:02,767 --> 00:27:03,300
-Whoa!

670
00:27:03,333 --> 00:27:05,933
That's what's going on!

671
00:27:05,967 --> 00:27:06,933
-OK, let's see.

672
00:27:06,967 --> 00:27:10,367
I'll take his wallet,
and his Echinacea, oh,

673
00:27:10,400 --> 00:27:12,333
and his goat cheese.

674
00:27:12,367 --> 00:27:13,033
Should I?

675
00:27:13,067 --> 00:27:15,800
Yes, I'll take his '70s watch.

676
00:27:15,833 --> 00:27:18,533
-You know, maybe I'm-- maybe
I'm not meant for this.

677
00:27:18,567 --> 00:27:22,133
Maybe I'm meant
for something else.

678
00:27:22,167 --> 00:27:24,033
-Maybe.

679
00:27:24,067 --> 00:27:29,167
-Sister Superior says that
I'm having a crisis of faith.

680
00:27:29,200 --> 00:27:30,033
[IMITATING BELCHING]

681
00:27:30,067 --> 00:27:31,433
-Maybe.

682
00:27:31,467 --> 00:27:32,867
-Well, what do you think?

683
00:27:32,900 --> 00:27:36,033
-Uh, I think I like
the Haagen Dazs better.

684
00:27:36,067 --> 00:27:37,367
-Maybe.

685
00:27:37,400 --> 00:27:38,333
-Come on!

686
00:27:38,367 --> 00:27:40,933
I'm looking for some
counseling, here, Fred.

687
00:27:40,967 --> 00:27:43,233
-Hey, I cut the meat, you know?

688
00:27:43,267 --> 00:27:45,900
Personally, I think you're
getting a little stupid

689
00:27:45,933 --> 00:27:47,800
about that kid that
bought the farm.

690
00:27:47,833 --> 00:27:48,767
-Hm?

691
00:27:48,800 --> 00:27:50,933
-Remember Jimmy Ho?

692
00:27:50,967 --> 00:27:52,367
Remember Lena Melcher?Ca

693
00:27:52,400 --> 00:27:53,500
-I heard about Terry.

694
00:27:53,533 --> 00:27:54,300
-Mink stole!

695
00:27:54,333 --> 00:27:54,833
-Sorry.

696
00:27:54,867 --> 00:27:56,500
-How's our guest?

697
00:27:56,533 --> 00:27:57,367
-Unconscious.

698
00:27:57,400 --> 00:27:58,600
Look what I found.

699
00:27:58,633 --> 00:28:00,100
-Calista Flockhart's belt.

700
00:28:00,133 --> 00:28:01,100
-Hm?

701
00:28:01,133 --> 00:28:03,200
Maybe he was into some
kind of bondage thing.

702
00:28:03,233 --> 00:28:04,800
-Smart guy.

703
00:28:04,833 --> 00:28:07,233
I patched up what I
could without x-rays.

704
00:28:07,267 --> 00:28:08,767
I'll know more tomorrow.

705
00:28:08,800 --> 00:28:11,067
-Well, why don't you
have a seat, nurse?

706
00:28:11,100 --> 00:28:11,567
-Yeah, come on.

707
00:28:11,600 --> 00:28:12,067
Sit down.

708
00:28:12,100 --> 00:28:12,967
-Nah, no time.

709
00:28:13,000 --> 00:28:14,300
I gotta get back to the clinic.

710
00:28:14,333 --> 00:28:16,200
Terrible habit, girl.

711
00:28:16,233 --> 00:28:17,833
-Hey, not on the floor!

712
00:28:17,867 --> 00:28:19,033
-It's good to have
you back, Ann.

713
00:28:19,067 --> 00:28:19,900
-Thanks.

714
00:28:19,933 --> 00:28:23,000
-I'll stop by
after my shift, OK?

715
00:28:23,033 --> 00:28:23,500
Bye.

716
00:28:23,533 --> 00:28:24,867
-Bye.

717
00:28:24,900 --> 00:28:26,167
-Hey, you want something, Max?

718
00:28:26,200 --> 00:28:28,400
-Uncle Fred says you
don't have a husband.

719
00:28:28,433 --> 00:28:30,633
Uncle Fred says, you should sh--
you're gonna shave your head

720
00:28:30,667 --> 00:28:31,500
and turn into a penguin.

721
00:28:31,533 --> 00:28:32,000
-Hm?

722
00:28:32,033 --> 00:28:32,833
-A penguin?

723
00:28:32,867 --> 00:28:33,700
-Can I watch?

724
00:28:33,733 --> 00:28:35,300
-It was a metaphor.

725
00:28:35,333 --> 00:28:36,733
-He says you don't
know what you're doing.

726
00:28:36,767 --> 00:28:37,567
He says--

727
00:28:37,600 --> 00:28:39,500
-Max, it's time
you got to bed now.

728
00:28:39,533 --> 00:28:40,867
Go brush your teeth.

729
00:28:40,900 --> 00:28:41,667
Go on.

730
00:28:41,700 --> 00:28:42,233
Say goodnight.

731
00:28:42,267 --> 00:28:43,033
-Goodnight.

732
00:28:43,067 --> 00:28:44,067
-Goodnight, Mom and Dad.

733
00:28:44,100 --> 00:28:45,300
-You're right, you know.

734
00:28:45,333 --> 00:28:46,500
-Aw, come on, Annie.

735
00:28:46,533 --> 00:28:47,400
I was just talking.

736
00:28:47,433 --> 00:28:49,200
-I mean, two days
ago, I was so sure.

737
00:28:49,233 --> 00:28:49,900
-And what?

738
00:28:49,933 --> 00:28:51,400
Today you don't know nothing?

739
00:28:51,433 --> 00:28:53,867
-It's hard being a
nun with a family.

740
00:28:53,900 --> 00:28:58,767
-Look, when we met, you
were hiding from a pimp.

741
00:28:58,800 --> 00:29:00,500
You had just did a
month in the joint.

742
00:29:00,533 --> 00:29:02,367
You were suicidal and addicted.

743
00:29:02,400 --> 00:29:03,867
-And you threw it all away.

744
00:29:03,900 --> 00:29:06,300
-Keeping you in here was hard.

745
00:29:06,333 --> 00:29:11,333
-When Lena was killed by some
guy wired up on the drugs

746
00:29:11,367 --> 00:29:12,533
he bought from me.

747
00:29:12,567 --> 00:29:14,933
-Aw, come off it, Annie.

748
00:29:14,967 --> 00:29:16,000
-It's like I pulled the trigger.

749
00:29:16,033 --> 00:29:17,033
-But you didn't.

750
00:29:17,067 --> 00:29:17,867
He did.

751
00:29:17,900 --> 00:29:19,433
You came here.

752
00:29:19,467 --> 00:29:21,100
You got clean.

753
00:29:21,133 --> 00:29:24,033
You helped other girls off
the junk and off the street.

754
00:29:24,067 --> 00:29:24,833
-Hmph!

755
00:29:24,867 --> 00:29:26,100
-That means something, Annie.

756
00:29:26,133 --> 00:29:28,467
-It means great service
and low, low prices.

757
00:29:32,533 --> 00:29:36,600
-[SIGH] I was a great hooker.

758
00:29:36,633 --> 00:29:38,067
[SIGH]

759
00:29:38,100 --> 00:29:40,467
-I'm gonna go up north
and visit and aunt.

760
00:29:40,500 --> 00:29:42,533
-She lives on an "aunt" farm.

761
00:29:42,567 --> 00:29:45,633
-Can you take care of that guy?

762
00:29:45,667 --> 00:29:46,533
-Listen, kid.

763
00:29:46,567 --> 00:29:48,933
Everything's gonna
work out just fine.

764
00:29:48,967 --> 00:29:50,300
You'll see.

765
00:29:50,333 --> 00:29:52,300
-Uh, what if God was one of us?

766
00:29:52,333 --> 00:29:54,833
-I hope so.

767
00:29:54,867 --> 00:29:56,867
-Promise Margarine--
a new kind of spread.

768
00:29:59,733 --> 00:30:00,533
-Our guest is awake?

769
00:30:00,567 --> 00:30:01,367
-Yep.

770
00:30:01,400 --> 00:30:02,567
-How's he doing?

771
00:30:02,600 --> 00:30:03,200
-OK.

772
00:30:03,233 --> 00:30:04,567
I couldn't talk to him.

773
00:30:04,600 --> 00:30:07,433
English, Spanish,
he doesn't talk.

774
00:30:07,467 --> 00:30:08,933
But I think he understands.

775
00:30:08,967 --> 00:30:10,600
I left him in the day-care room.

776
00:30:10,633 --> 00:30:11,167
-Hm.

777
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:12,267
Let's go have a look.

778
00:30:12,300 --> 00:30:14,267
-They must go through a lot
of zoobas in this house.

779
00:30:14,300 --> 00:30:15,333
-Mm, hm.

780
00:30:15,367 --> 00:30:17,400
-And maybe he can tell us
what this thing is for.

781
00:30:17,433 --> 00:30:18,367
-Yeah.

782
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:19,733
-Where are you going?

783
00:30:19,767 --> 00:30:21,500
-I'm gonna go to
my room and pack.

784
00:30:21,533 --> 00:30:23,100
I want to get on
the road by 12:00.

785
00:30:23,133 --> 00:30:24,167
-Oh, no.

786
00:30:24,200 --> 00:30:25,767
Aren't you gonna stay and
help us with this guy?

787
00:30:25,800 --> 00:30:26,333
He's yours.

788
00:30:26,367 --> 00:30:27,400
-Yeah, Sister, come on.

789
00:30:27,433 --> 00:30:29,133
You're good at this kinda thing.

790
00:30:29,167 --> 00:30:30,933
-They don't get the
all-kickboxing station.

791
00:30:33,533 --> 00:30:36,100
-Sorry, I ate your
breakfast on the way in.

792
00:30:36,133 --> 00:30:38,367
[MUSIC]

793
00:30:38,400 --> 00:30:40,367
-It's hard to sample
off the radio.

794
00:30:40,400 --> 00:30:41,800
-Mm.

795
00:30:41,833 --> 00:30:45,133
[STATIC]

796
00:30:45,167 --> 00:30:46,500
-[IMITATING_PASSINGóGAS]
Oh, sorry.

797
00:30:46,533 --> 00:30:47,967
That's not very
appetizing, is it.

798
00:30:51,900 --> 00:30:53,833
-I just thought of a
great joke from Nun-sense.

799
00:30:59,367 --> 00:31:03,300
-Good thing we
switched places, there.

800
00:31:03,333 --> 00:31:03,800
-Hi, there.

801
00:31:03,833 --> 00:31:05,033
I'm Fred.

802
00:31:05,067 --> 00:31:05,767
That's Romero.

803
00:31:05,800 --> 00:31:07,133
And that's Sister Ann.

804
00:31:07,167 --> 00:31:10,200
-I assume you've met
your corn with pimentos?

805
00:31:10,233 --> 00:31:11,967
