1127
00:43:01,300 --> 00:43:01,767
-Aah!

1128
00:43:01,800 --> 00:43:03,167
-Ooh!

1129
00:43:03,200 --> 00:43:03,833
-Hey!

1130
00:43:03,867 --> 00:43:05,967
-Yeah, you tried to kill us!

1131
00:43:06,000 --> 00:43:07,867
-What the--

1132
00:43:07,900 --> 00:43:09,300
-No!

1133
00:43:09,333 --> 00:43:11,233
I didn't.

1134
00:43:11,267 --> 00:43:12,100
No!

1135
00:43:12,133 --> 00:43:13,067
Never.

1136
00:43:13,100 --> 00:43:13,700
-Yes, you did.

1137
00:43:13,733 --> 00:43:15,300
Ooh!

1138
00:43:15,333 --> 00:43:17,800
-Well, I just think
this changes everything.

1139
00:43:17,833 --> 00:43:20,367
I suppose there's other times
you tried to kill us, too!

1140
00:43:20,400 --> 00:43:21,067
[ALARM SOUNDING]

1141
00:43:21,100 --> 00:43:22,400
-Oh, now we have movie signs.

1142
00:43:22,433 --> 00:43:23,333
Can I even trust that?

1143
00:43:23,367 --> 00:43:24,333
I don't know!

1144
00:43:35,633 --> 00:43:37,600
-Sister Ann, are you all right?

1145
00:43:37,633 --> 00:43:38,500
-I can't believe this!

1146
00:43:38,533 --> 00:43:39,000
-Yeah.

1147
00:43:39,033 --> 00:43:40,467
I mean, wow!

1148
00:43:40,500 --> 00:43:41,933
-Ever since yesterday,
at the burial,

1149
00:43:41,967 --> 00:43:44,667
I've been asking myself--

1150
00:43:44,700 --> 00:43:46,300
-How much to undertakers make?

1151
00:43:46,333 --> 00:43:47,633
- --what I missed.

1152
00:43:47,667 --> 00:43:49,633
-You didn't miss
anything, my dear.

1153
00:43:49,667 --> 00:43:51,733
It wasn't your fault.

1154
00:43:51,767 --> 00:43:53,567
-How come I wasn't taken?

1155
00:43:53,600 --> 00:43:55,133
-Because you weren't.

1156
00:43:55,167 --> 00:43:55,867
And that's that.

1157
00:43:55,900 --> 00:43:57,900
-So shut your trap!

1158
00:43:57,933 --> 00:44:02,833
-I don't know if I'm gonna
take my final vows next week.

1159
00:44:02,867 --> 00:44:04,667
-I have a nail appointment.

1160
00:44:04,700 --> 00:44:05,733
-Because of Terry Jo?

1161
00:44:05,767 --> 00:44:06,667
That's what this is--

1162
00:44:06,700 --> 00:44:08,500
-You knew what I was
before I came here.

1163
00:44:08,533 --> 00:44:09,433
-Hm?

1164
00:44:09,467 --> 00:44:11,367
-Sister William looks concerned.

1165
00:44:11,400 --> 00:44:13,033
-Well, you had a record.

1166
00:44:13,067 --> 00:44:14,167
So did Mary Magdalene.

1167
00:44:14,200 --> 00:44:17,033
-I was a whore doing
tricks in back allies.

1168
00:44:17,067 --> 00:44:17,533
-Sister Ann.

1169
00:44:17,567 --> 00:44:18,367
-I sold drugs.

1170
00:44:18,400 --> 00:44:19,767
-Sister Ann, that was then.

1171
00:44:19,800 --> 00:44:20,567
-This was then, too.

1172
00:44:20,600 --> 00:44:21,700
It's weird.

1173
00:44:21,733 --> 00:44:23,300
-I'm very proud of you now.

1174
00:44:23,333 --> 00:44:25,533
-You bring in a lot of
cash to the convent.

1175
00:44:25,567 --> 00:44:26,133
-I'm not.

1176
00:44:28,867 --> 00:44:33,067
-Well, then we have a
problem, here, don't we?

1177
00:44:33,100 --> 00:44:36,833
-She was smart, Sister.

1178
00:44:36,867 --> 00:44:39,233
Good, tough--

1179
00:44:39,267 --> 00:44:41,067
-She was built Ford tough.

1180
00:44:41,100 --> 00:44:42,233
-Sister--

1181
00:44:42,267 --> 00:44:43,900
-I should have been there
for her when she needed me.

1182
00:44:43,933 --> 00:44:46,133
-Sister Ann, why don't
you take the weekend--

1183
00:44:46,167 --> 00:44:47,767
-Go out to the
track, or something.

1184
00:44:47,800 --> 00:44:49,733
- --visit your
friends and family.

1185
00:44:49,767 --> 00:44:52,833
Though perfection is not
one of the requirements,

1186
00:44:52,867 --> 00:44:55,167
faith is, Sister.

1187
00:44:55,200 --> 00:44:56,533
Do you believe in signs?

1188
00:44:56,567 --> 00:44:58,700
-I believe in "yield
from [? right."

1189
00:44:58,733 --> 00:45:00,900
-I guess I do.

1190
00:45:00,933 --> 00:45:01,600
-Really?

1191
00:45:01,633 --> 00:45:02,467
I-- I don't know what to say.

1192
00:45:02,500 --> 00:45:03,833
I thought you were
gonna say, no.

1193
00:45:03,867 --> 00:45:05,033
-Keep your eyes open.

1194
00:45:05,067 --> 00:45:06,433
-You can't trust these nuns.

1195
00:45:06,467 --> 00:45:08,600
-God always answers prayers.

1196
00:45:08,633 --> 00:45:09,533
-But only from Catholics!

1197
00:45:13,667 --> 00:45:16,333
-We'll take a brief break
from my flashback, now.

1198
00:45:16,367 --> 00:45:18,333
-What about the tracker?

1199
00:45:18,367 --> 00:45:20,900
What happens now?

1200
00:45:20,933 --> 00:45:25,033
-The tracker will
rest, then go back--

1201
00:45:25,067 --> 00:45:26,833
-What was I talking about?

1202
00:45:26,867 --> 00:45:29,433
- --to where it first found us.

1203
00:45:29,467 --> 00:45:30,867
-Is he talking about a warwolf?

1204
00:45:30,900 --> 00:45:34,533
-I don't believe this!

1205
00:45:34,567 --> 00:45:35,800
(IMITATING TWEETY
BIRD) Dis is a city.

1206
00:45:35,833 --> 00:45:39,500
12 million puddy tats.

1207
00:45:39,533 --> 00:45:40,767
-Are you going back?

1208
00:45:40,800 --> 00:45:41,900
-Yes.

1209
00:45:41,933 --> 00:45:44,233
-But the tracker
has your scent now.

1210
00:45:44,267 --> 00:45:45,000
-Tough!

1211
00:45:45,033 --> 00:45:46,167
-He'll have to deal with it!

1212
00:45:46,200 --> 00:45:49,833
-If I go with you,
it will find me.

1213
00:45:49,867 --> 00:45:52,233
-Well, then you better
get back on the train.

1214
00:45:52,267 --> 00:45:55,767
-Say, by the way,
what is "KISS"?

1215
00:45:55,800 --> 00:45:58,100
-I do not understand.

1216
00:45:58,133 --> 00:46:00,200
-This is something I have to do.

1217
00:46:00,233 --> 00:46:03,133
I'd like to give you
some big words of wisdom,

1218
00:46:03,167 --> 00:46:04,967
but I just don't have any.

1219
00:46:05,000 --> 00:46:06,567
My mind's blank.

1220
00:46:06,600 --> 00:46:08,533
You do what you have to do.

1221
00:46:08,567 --> 00:46:09,533
Goodbye.

1222
00:46:09,567 --> 00:46:14,033
-We don't have a permit
to shoot on curb.

1223
00:46:14,067 --> 00:46:16,533
(IMITATING STEVE MARTIN)
Am I a wild and crazy guy?

1224
00:46:16,567 --> 00:46:18,700
What are you doing?

1225
00:46:18,733 --> 00:46:20,367
-Doing what I believe to.

1226
00:46:20,400 --> 00:46:22,300
-Is that OK at you?

1227
00:46:22,333 --> 00:46:24,633
-And what's that?

1228
00:46:24,667 --> 00:46:26,067
-Going with you.

1229
00:46:26,100 --> 00:46:29,633
-Look, let's get this straight.

1230
00:46:29,667 --> 00:46:30,467
I work alone.

1231
00:46:30,500 --> 00:46:32,500
-I nun outta my home.

1232
00:46:32,533 --> 00:46:34,233
-Alone!

1233
00:46:34,267 --> 00:46:35,100
By myself!

1234
00:46:35,133 --> 00:46:37,567
I want to be alone!

1235
00:46:37,600 --> 00:46:43,367
-Better is a neighbor that is
near than a brother far off.

1236
00:46:43,400 --> 00:46:45,767
-Oh, that's from one of
them "Chicken Soup" books.

1237
00:46:45,800 --> 00:46:46,900
-I don't want to
talk about this.

1238
00:46:49,600 --> 00:46:50,867
-Would you button my shirt?

1239
00:46:54,067 --> 00:46:55,567
-I'm going to call
Sister Gary and see

1240
00:46:55,600 --> 00:46:56,767
