1241
00:46:56,800 --> 00:46:58,300
[PHONE RINGING]

1242
00:46:58,333 --> 00:47:01,300
RECORDING: The number you have
reached is not in service.

1243
00:47:01,333 --> 00:47:02,467
-Oh, Vatican!

1244
00:47:02,500 --> 00:47:05,467
Pay you phone bill!

1245
00:47:05,500 --> 00:47:07,133
-Heaven's a mess, isn't it?

1246
00:47:07,167 --> 00:47:08,133
-I don't know.

1247
00:47:08,167 --> 00:47:09,067
I like it.

1248
00:47:09,100 --> 00:47:12,767
"The Alien and the
Nun," this fall on CBS.

1249
00:47:12,800 --> 00:47:14,767
-How many people
got murdered today?

1250
00:47:14,800 --> 00:47:15,467
Huh?

1251
00:47:15,500 --> 00:47:16,567
Or raped?

1252
00:47:16,600 --> 00:47:17,067
Beaten?

1253
00:47:17,100 --> 00:47:19,767
Oh, missing?

1254
00:47:19,800 --> 00:47:21,167
-You're upset.

1255
00:47:21,200 --> 00:47:22,333
-Yeah, I'm upset.

1256
00:47:22,367 --> 00:47:23,567
-Didn't my acting convey that?

1257
00:47:23,600 --> 00:47:25,100
-But you want to
help your friends.

1258
00:47:25,133 --> 00:47:27,367
-And that's different,
I know them.

1259
00:47:27,400 --> 00:47:28,967
-You don't know me.

1260
00:47:29,000 --> 00:47:31,433
You helped me.

1261
00:47:31,467 --> 00:47:34,867
Greater love has
no man than this;

1262
00:47:34,900 --> 00:47:37,733
than a man lay down his life--

1263
00:47:37,767 --> 00:47:38,267
-Heard it!

1264
00:47:38,300 --> 00:47:39,800
- --for his friend.

1265
00:47:39,833 --> 00:47:40,367
-Ugh!

1266
00:47:40,400 --> 00:47:42,733
I got to get outta here.

1267
00:47:42,767 --> 00:47:45,767
-Should we be worried
about our friends?

1268
00:47:45,800 --> 00:47:48,000
-That is what I want to be.

1269
00:47:48,033 --> 00:47:48,700
-What?

1270
00:47:48,733 --> 00:47:50,533
-A man.

1271
00:47:50,567 --> 00:47:51,933
-You are a man.

1272
00:47:51,967 --> 00:47:53,100
-No.

1273
00:47:53,133 --> 00:47:55,900
I mean, greater love.

1274
00:47:55,933 --> 00:47:58,533
that kind of man.

1275
00:47:58,567 --> 00:48:00,400
-Well, you better be
careful what you wish for.

1276
00:48:00,433 --> 00:48:01,833
-Sister Mary Despair.

1277
00:48:10,100 --> 00:48:11,000
-Ah, life is good!

1278
00:48:11,033 --> 00:48:13,933
I live in Maui and I
got a "Monster" mag.

1279
00:48:13,967 --> 00:48:16,267
Ha, ha.

1280
00:48:16,300 --> 00:48:17,633
[GROWLING]

1281
00:48:17,667 --> 00:48:20,467
-(SINGING DRUNKENLY) Wasted
away again in Margaritaville.

1282
00:48:23,833 --> 00:48:26,733
-Ew!

1283
00:48:26,767 --> 00:48:29,600
He has the live, supple
figure out James Doohan.

1284
00:48:33,167 --> 00:48:36,233
[GROWLING]

1285
00:48:36,267 --> 00:48:38,033
-A man was snapped at by a
forced-perspective puppet,

1286
00:48:38,067 --> 00:48:39,133
today.

1287
00:48:39,167 --> 00:48:40,567
-We're going on the assumption
that some animal out

1288
00:48:40,600 --> 00:48:42,467
of the hills has
gone on a rampage.

1289
00:48:42,500 --> 00:48:43,300
-Hm, hm.

1290
00:48:43,333 --> 00:48:45,300
-The body found
here at Third Street

1291
00:48:45,333 --> 00:48:47,467
makes four deaths in six hours.

1292
00:48:47,500 --> 00:48:49,867
This creature knows
where it's going.

1293
00:48:49,900 --> 00:48:52,533
I want cars posted
all along this route.

1294
00:48:52,567 --> 00:48:54,367
-Make 'em all Tercels.

1295
00:48:54,400 --> 00:48:56,767
-Stay in close radio
contact at all times.

1296
00:48:56,800 --> 00:48:57,633
Let's go.

1297
00:48:57,667 --> 00:49:00,800
[GULP]

1298
00:49:00,833 --> 00:49:01,800
-Is God out there?

1299
00:49:01,833 --> 00:49:03,433
-He is (SHOUTING)
out there, man!

1300
00:49:03,467 --> 00:49:04,133
Whew!

1301
00:49:04,167 --> 00:49:06,233
-God of Gods, and King of Kings.

1302
00:49:06,267 --> 00:49:08,233
-You don't even know what
you're saying, do you?

1303
00:49:08,267 --> 00:49:09,667
-[GIBBERISH]

1304
00:49:09,700 --> 00:49:10,667
-You don't.

1305
00:49:10,700 --> 00:49:12,867
-[GIBBERISH]

1306
00:49:12,900 --> 00:49:13,867
-What's out there?

1307
00:49:13,900 --> 00:49:16,133
Is heaven out there?

1308
00:49:16,167 --> 00:49:17,100
-Earth is heaven.

1309
00:49:17,133 --> 00:49:17,800
-Thanks to Olestra.

1310
00:49:20,833 --> 00:49:22,400
-And the Supreme Being is what?

1311
00:49:22,433 --> 00:49:24,133
-Well, it's not Earl Holliman.

1312
00:49:24,167 --> 00:49:26,600
-Handlers-- masters.

1313
00:49:26,633 --> 00:49:27,867
-No, no, no, no.

1314
00:49:27,900 --> 00:49:28,500
Not them.

1315
00:49:28,533 --> 00:49:29,600
Greater than them.

1316
00:49:29,633 --> 00:49:32,933
-(WITH BAVARIAN ACCENT) What
is your word for boring?

1317
00:49:32,967 --> 00:49:34,000
-Ha!

1318
00:49:34,033 --> 00:49:36,833
If the movie's dragging,
then they show us soccer.

1319
00:49:36,867 --> 00:49:39,100
Good!

1320
00:49:39,133 --> 00:49:39,800
-Soccer's my game.

1321
00:49:39,833 --> 00:49:41,433
I've no arms, ya see!

1322
00:49:41,467 --> 00:49:42,300
-Aah!

1323
00:49:42,333 --> 00:49:43,567
-Aah!

1324
00:49:43,600 --> 00:49:44,067
[PHONE RINGING]

1325
00:49:44,100 --> 00:49:45,633
-Puffy Hat Police.

1326
00:49:45,667 --> 00:49:47,100
-Western Division,
Officer Fry speaking.

1327
00:49:47,133 --> 00:49:49,033
How may I help you?

1328
00:49:49,067 --> 00:49:50,167
-Hello.

1329
00:49:50,200 --> 00:49:52,200
-This is Mail Boxes Etc,
people really need our boxes!

1330
00:49:52,233 --> 00:49:53,233
FRY (ON PHONE): Stay calm, sir.

1331
00:49:53,267 --> 00:49:56,000
